From: zig-feedstock
Subject: [PATCH] mingw: add _fpreset stub for arm (thumb + aarch64)

_fpreset is defined only in CRT_fp10.c (x86-only via mingw32_x86_src). It
is called by crt_handler.c, tlsthrd.c, crtexe.c, and winpthreads/thread.c
which are compiled for all arches. On aarch64, lld-link cannot auto-import
_fpreset from ucrtbase.dll because BL instructions generate
IMAGE_REL_ARM64_BRANCH26 relocations that cannot be patched to indirect
import thunks. Provide a no-op stub for arm targets (no x87 FPU to reset).

drop-when: zig upstream adds a fpreset arm stub to mingw32_arm_src

diff --git a/lib/libc/mingw/crt/fpreset_arm.c b/lib/libc/mingw/crt/fpreset_arm.c
new file mode 100644
--- /dev/null
+++ b/lib/libc/mingw/crt/fpreset_arm.c
@@ -0,0 +1,12 @@
+/* No-op _fpreset stub for ARM (thumb + aarch64).
+ *
+ * CRT_fp10.c provides _fpreset for x86 via `__asm__ ("fninit")` (x87 FPU
+ * instruction) and is in mingw32_x86_src. ARM has no x87 FPU. References
+ * to _fpreset from generic sources (crt_handler.c, tlsthrd.c, crtexe.c,
+ * winpthreads/thread.c) need a resolved symbol on arm targets -- they get
+ * one here. lld-link cannot auto-import _fpreset from a DLL on aarch64
+ * because the BL (branch) instruction generates IMAGE_REL_ARM64_BRANCH26
+ * relocations that cannot be patched to indirect import thunks.
+ */
+void _fpreset(void) {}
+void fpreset(void) {}
diff --git a/src/libs/mingw.zig b/src/libs/mingw.zig
--- a/src/libs/mingw.zig
+++ b/src/libs/mingw.zig
@@ -902,4 +902,5 @@
 const mingw32_arm_src = [_][]const u8{
     // mingwex
     "math" ++ path.sep_str ++ "arm-common" ++ path.sep_str ++ "ldexpl.c",
+    "crt" ++ path.sep_str ++ "fpreset_arm.c",
 };
